IMPORT prelude

-- Arkansas Code 26-51-201(a)(3) -- the income tax rate tables for individuals, trusts and estates, tax years from 2024.
--
-- Edition: Acts 2024 (2nd Ex. Sess.), No. 1, s 1 (approved 19 June 2024, emergency clause), which amends 26-51-201(a)(3)
-- "to read as follows", as published by the Arkansas General Assembly and deposited at
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ar-acts-2024-2nd-ex-sess-act-1.txt
-- with the tables as enacted transcribed in ../../registers/source-bundle/ar-acts-2024-2nd-ex-sess-act-1.formulas.md
-- (the plain text loses the Act's strike-through). The Bureau of Legislative Research's lists of Code sections amended in
-- the 2025 Regular and 2026 Fiscal Sessions show no later amendment of 26-51-201(a)(3).
--
-- The Arkansas Code itself is not deposited (its only online publisher, LexisNexis, served a CAPTCHA). So: net income, the
-- rest of s 26-51-201 (including any inflation adjustment of these tables), the personal tax credits, deductions, residence
-- and filing are all outside this encoding. Net income is an INPUT.
--
-- In: s 26-51-201(a)(3)(A), (B), (C).
-- Out: tax years before 2024 (`not covered`); everything else in Chapter 51.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING, from the seat of the individual taxpayer. Expected values in the case file are hand-written. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT TAX ADVICE.

§ `Ark. Code 26-51-201(a)(3) -- the tax on net income, tax years from 2024`

§§ `What this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- earlier subdivisions of s 26-51-201(a) are not deposited
    `the rate tables for tax years before 2024 are not deposited`

DECLARE `Answer` IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `amount`  IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `(3)(A) -- net income of $89,600 or less`

-- "Every resident, individual, trust, or estate having net income less than or equal to ... ($89,600) shall determine the
-- amount of income tax due ... in accordance with the table": 0% to $5,299; 2% from $5,300 to $10,599; 3% from $10,600 to
-- $15,099; 3.4% from $15,100 to $24,999; 3.9% from $25,000 to $89,600. Each rate is read as applying to the part of net
-- income within its row (NOTES.md finding 2).
GIVEN `net income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax under table A` MEANS
        (2%   TIMES `the part between` `net income` 5299 10599)
    PLUS (3%  TIMES `the part between` `net income` 10599 15099)
    PLUS (3.4% TIMES `the part between` `net income` 15099 24999)
    PLUS (3.9% TIMES `the part between` `net income` 24999 89600)

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER, `bottom` IS A NUMBER, `top` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part between` MEANS
    max 0 ((min `amount` `top`) MINUS `bottom`)

§§ `(3)(B) -- net income over $89,600`

-- 2% from $0 to $4,500; 3.9% from $4,501 and above.
GIVEN `net income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax under table B` MEANS
    (2% TIMES min `net income` 4500) PLUS (3.9% TIMES max 0 (`net income` MINUS 4500))

§§ `(3)(C) -- the bracket adjustment, $89,601 to $92,700`

-- The tax under (B) is reduced "by deducting a bracket adjustment amount in accordance with the table": $310 for net
-- income from $89,601 to $89,700, then $10 less for each further $100, to $10 for $92,601 to $92,700, and $0 from $92,701.
-- Written as that arithmetic, which reproduces each of the table's 32 rows (formulas sidecar).
GIVEN `net income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the bracket adjustment amount` MEANS
    IF `net income` LESS THAN 89601 OR `net income` GREATER THAN 92700
    THEN 0
    ELSE 310 MINUS (10 TIMES FLOOR ((`net income` MINUS 89601) DIVIDED BY 100))

§§ `The tax`

GIVEN `net income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax under subdivision (a)(3)` MEANS
    IF `net income` AT MOST 89600
    THEN `the tax under table A` `net income`
    ELSE `the tax under table B` `net income` MINUS `the bracket adjustment amount` `net income`

-- =====================================================================================================================
§ `Questions for the taxpayer`

@export What is my Arkansas income tax on my net income, before credits, for a tax year from 2024 (Ark. Code 26-51-201(a)(3), as set by Acts 2024 (2nd Ex. Sess.), No. 1)?
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The tax year, e.g. 2025
      `my net income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Arkansas net income for the year (after deductions), in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`What is my Arkansas tax on my net income` MEANS
    IF `tax year` LESS THAN 2024
    THEN `not covered` `the rate tables for tax years before 2024 are not deposited`
    ELSE `answered` (`the tax under subdivision (a)(3)` `my net income`)

@export What bracket adjustment reduces my Arkansas tax, for net income from $89,601 to $92,700 in a tax year from 2024 (Ark. Code 26-51-201(a)(3)(C))? 0 outside that range.
GIVEN `my net income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Arkansas net income for the year, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What bracket adjustment do I get` MEANS
    `the bracket adjustment amount` `my net income`
